    "narrative": "For the May 31st slate, our offensive engine is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both benefiting from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms in favorable park environments. **Jackson Merrill** remains our premier play, as he maximizes his scoring potential against Littell despite a slight discount for the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop-time. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives in his 2-hole slot against Canning; the +14% dynamic platoon boost makes him an essential start. **Gunnar Henderson** (71.73) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.83) round out our tier-one options, with **Gunnar Henderson** specifically overcoming a tough matchup against Miles thanks to a significant park-factor lift that offsets the negative SP skill adjustment.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes the scarcity of stolen bases and optimal batting order leverage, leading to a difficult \"marginal\" decision for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95) and **Miguel Vargas** (57.84). While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a challenging 3.09 xERA arm in Bradish, his base projection and park-adjusted ceiling kept him in the UTIL spot over **Brayan Rocchio** (43.08), whose floor is suppressed by his spot in the 9-hole. **Sam Antonacci** (61.66) is a high-value play today; his strong 1-hole positioning and impressive xwOBA justify starting him over any available bench options. We remain cautious regarding **Liam Hicks** (41.06), whose reliance on a platoon edge is tempered by facing McLean, a pitcher showing legitimate efficiency (3.03 xERA).\n\nWe are currently managing a thin bench due to injuries to **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin**. With those assets sidelined, our depth options\u2014**Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Dominic Smith**\u2014were evaluated but ultimately passed over in favor of the current starting nine. The optimizer prioritized the BvP and platoon efficiency of **Andy Pages** (64.70) against Painter, as his current form provides more immediate value than the remaining bench reserve. No weather-related risks are flagged for today, but we will continue to monitor any late scratches, particularly for **Liam Hicks** and the bottom-order utility spots, to preserve our remaining game caps.",
